<title>HONG KONG: Hotel deal pulls New World up from low.</title>
<headline>Hotel deal pulls New World up from low.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of New World Development Co Ltd were pulled up from lows on buying fueled by news that the company had agreed to sell its hotel unit Renaissance Hotel Group NV to Doubletree Corp, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Even though the (New World) shares fell in line with the overall market's plunge this morning, the news was seen as positive on the shares' price in longer run,&quot; said Anthony Mak, sales director at Vickers Ballas.</p>
<p>New World shares stood at HK$52.25 in late morning, up from its morning low of HK$51.00 per share but unchanged with its Tuesday close, while the Hang Seng index was down 1.40 percent.</p>
